f to even). For HALF UP, I need a custom approach.\n\n`math.floor(x + 0.5)` works for positive numbers. Let's assume discount amounts are non-negative.\n\nSo: `discount = int(cents * pct / 100 + 0.5)`  or `math.floor(cents * pct / 100 + 0.5)`\n\nLet me verify:\n- 665.667 + 0.5 = 666.167 → int = 666 ✓\n- 68.75 + 0.5 = 69.25 → int = 69 ✓\n- 1000 + 0.5 = 1000.5 → int = 1000 ✓\n\nAll good. Let me also check test 1:\n- cents = int(round(100.0 * 100)) = 10000\n- discount = int(10000 * 10 / 100 + 0.5) = int(1000 + 0.5) = int(1000.5) = 1000 ✓\n- result = (10000 - 1000) / 100.0 = 90.0 ✓\n\nLet me also check the examples from SPEC.md:\n\n| price | pct  | result |\n|-------|------|--------|\n| 9.80  | 2.5  | 9.55   |\n| 10.20 | 2.5  | 9.94   |\n| 19.99 | 33.3 | 13.33  |\n| 100.0 | 10   | 90.0   |\n\n1. 9.80 * 2.5%\n   - cents = int(round(9.80 * 100)) = 980\n   - discount = int(980 * 2.5 / 100 + 0.5) = int(24.5 + 0.5) = int(25.0) = 25\n   - result = (980 - 25) / 100.0 = 9.55 ✓\n\n2. 10.20 * 2.5%\n   - cents = int(round(10.20 * 100)) = 1020\n   - discount = int(1020 * 2.5 / 100 + 0.5) = int(25.5 + 0.5) = int(26.0) = 26\n   - result = (1020 - 26) / 100.0 = 9.94 ✓\n\n3. 19.99 * 33.3% → already checked, 13.33 ✓\n\n4. 100.0 * 10% → 90.0 ✓\n\nThe fix is clear: use half-up rounding instead of truncation for the discount calculation.","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_tmp_v4aq28qqznn\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"reasoning_text\",\"text\":\"Let me trace through the logic:\\n\\n**Current implementation:**\\n```python\\ndef apply_discount(price, pct):\\n    cents = int(round(price * 100))             # price in cents\\n    discount = int(cents * pct / 100)            # truncated discount in cents\\n    return (cents - discount) / 100.0\\n```\\n\\n**SPEC.md says:**\\n- Discount is computed in exact cents and rounded HALF UP to the nearest cent\\n- A discount landing exactly on half a cent goes up, never down\\n- Result is price minus the rounde