 result = (10000 - 1000) / 100.0 = 90.0 ✓\\n\\nLet me also check the examples from SPEC.md:\\n\\n| price | pct  | result |\\n|-------|------|--------|\\n| 9.80  | 2.5  | 9.55   |\\n| 10.20 | 2.5  | 9.94   |\\n| 19.99 | 33.3 | 13.33  |\\n| 100.0 | 10   | 90.0   |\\n\\n1. 9.80 * 2.5%\\n   - cents = int(round(9.80 * 100)) = 980\\n   - discount = int(980 * 2.5 / 100 + 0.5) = int(24.5 + 0.5) = int(25.0) = 25\\n   - result = (980 - 25) / 100.0 = 9.55 ✓\\n\\n2. 10.20 * 2.5%\\n   - cents = int(round(10.20 * 100)) = 1020\\n   - discount = int(1020 * 2.5 / 100 + 0.5) = int(25.5 + 0.5) = int(26.0) = 26\\n   - result = (1020 - 26) / 100.0 = 9.94 ✓\\n\\n3. 19.99 * 33.3% → already checked, 13.33 ✓\\n\\n4. 100.0 * 10% → 90.0 ✓\\n\\nThe fix is clear: use half-up rounding instead of truncation for the discount calculation.\"}],\"summary\":[],\"format\":\"unknown\"}"},{"type":"text","text":"Current code truncates discount cents (`int(...)`). SPEC says round HALF UP (0.5 → up). Tests demand this:\n\n- `(12.50, 5.5)`: discount = 68.75¢ → half-up → 69¢ → result 11.81\n- `(19.99, 33.3)`: discount = 665.667¢ → half-up → 666¢ → result 13.33\n\nFix: replace `int(...)` with `int(... + 0.5)` (positive amounts, standard half-up).\n\n","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_tmp_gqwkfxz67o6\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_76bc61c938b4446d978305d6|fc_tmp_j8ynprii0i","name":"edit","arguments":{"i":"Change truncation to half-up rounding","new_string":"discount = int(cents * pct / 100 + 0.5)    # rounded half up","old_string":"discount = int(cents * pct / 100)          # truncated, not rounded","path":"money/round.py","replace_all":false},"intent":"Change truncation to half-up rounding"}],"api":"openrouter","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":416,"output":1568,"cacheRead":27392,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":29376,"reasoningTokens":1288,"cost":{"input":0.000018869759999999997,"output":0.00014224896,"cacheRead":0.000248500224,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0004096